                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "For such an old game I feel like it still hits all the right parts of a restaurant sim game. \n\nCampaign story that while definitely made for television is entertaining and challenging...check\nIngredient Management for quality improvements...check\nStaff skills, training, and management...check\nPhysical Restaurant Building management...check\nCooking Competitions and Tournaments...check\n\nOutside of not being able to control your own chef directly (hence it's a management simulator) this game really did everything really well. I feel like i'm still looking for a game that does all my desires for a restaurant management like this game. \n\nHighly recommend this game to anyone who has that itch to run a restaurant but not want the tiring cooking simulator niche that has become the more mainstream attempt at this sim.\n\n8/10 There's some glitchhyness that they've done a great job mitigating with patches. Game plays wonderfully and you enjoy most of your time playing. Can get a little repetitive and micro-managing sometimes but i've always found it in that perfect spot where it's challenging but not harsh.",
